# The warehouse example's entry module. It reads an order from a table,
# expands each line through a bill of materials (a bundle is made of other
# products, and of other bundles), looks each part's price up in a catalog
# table by its SKU, builds the priced lines into a list, prices it two ways at
# once (two tasks borrow the same list), prints both totals and a subtotal per
# category, writes a one-line report file, and reads the report back.
#
# What the checker and runtime guarantee here (docs/safety-guarantees.md):
# - `order` has 3 rows, so `fill` states `maxIterations 3`; fewer is rejected.
# - A SKU the catalog does not list is a value the program handles
#   (`catalog.find` raises `list.NotFound`, exit 7), not a missing price.
# - Bundles form a tree: `components` gives each bundle its parts, and a part
#   may be a bundle. `addOrderLine` walks it recursively (`maxRecursion 8`);
#   a bundle nested deeper than 4, or one that contains itself, is a handled
#   error (exit 9), never unbounded recursion.
# - An order may name a SKU once: `markSku` (the generic `markNew` at Int64)
#   records each SKU in a set, and a repeat is exit 8.
# - Subtotals per category live in a map from category name to cents and are
#   printed in the order categories first appear (D-62).
# - Both tasks hold `lines` from `start` to `join`, so nothing may change it
#   until both are joined, including after a `cancel`.
# - When the list total fails, the discount task is cancelled and still joined;
#   its outcome is observed, and a second failure is reported, not dropped.
# - `report` is written through an exclusive loan (`lendMutable`): writing
#   changes the handle's position, so no other activation may use it at once.
# - A file open for writing cannot be opened again, by any name, until it is
#   closed (D-52); so the report is closed on every path before it is read
#   back, and a failed write still closes it before giving up.
# - Every allocation goes into `store`. Before building the report line the
#   program asks `store` for room (`arena.ensure`) and stops with exit 6 if it
#   is short, instead of trapping halfway (D-55).
# - Each dropped failure names exactly the variants it drops (`suppresses`).
# - build.sem's authority is approved in authority.approved; asking for more
#   stops the program before it starts (D-53).
# - The report read back is checked for the discounted total it was written
#   with (`string.contains`) before it is printed.
# - The report's path and labels are module constants: immutable, typed, and
#   set before any operation runs (D-103).
#
# Exit codes: 0 done, 2 a line has a negative quantity, 3 the order is empty,
# 4 the report file could not be written or read back intact, 5 standard
# output failed, 6 no room left in `store` for the report, 7 the order names a
# SKU the catalog does not list, 8 the order names a SKU twice, 9 a bundle is
# nested too deep or contains itself.

warehouse is module
warehouse purpose "Price an order at list price and with a bulk discount, then write and read back a report"
warehouse path warehouse
warehouse imports standard.console
warehouse imports standard.fs
warehouse imports standard.string
warehouse imports standard.time
warehouse imports standard.arena
warehouse imports standard.list
warehouse imports standard.map
warehouse imports standard.set
warehouse imports standard.compare
warehouse imports standard.math
warehouse imports pricing
warehouse exports main

stdoutWriter is capability
stdoutWriter purpose "Authority to write lines to standard output"
stdoutWriter grants write console.stdout none

stderrWriter is capability
stderrWriter purpose "Authority to write notes to standard error"
stderrWriter grants write console.stderr none

reportFiles is capability
reportFiles purpose "Authority to write and read files in the working directory whose names start with warehouse-"
reportFiles grants write fs.files "warehouse-*"
reportFiles grants read fs.files "warehouse-*"

reportPath is constant
reportPath purpose "The report file, inside the scope `reportFiles` grants"
reportPath type String
reportPath value "warehouse-report.txt"

listLabel is constant
listLabel purpose "What the report writes before the list total"
listLabel type String
listLabel value "list="

discountLabel is constant
discountLabel purpose "What the report writes before the discounted total, and what reading it back looks for"
discountLabel type String
discountLabel value " discounted="

OrderLine is record
OrderLine purpose "One line as ordered: which product and how many"
OrderLine typeParameter none
OrderLine field sku Int64
OrderLine field quantity Int64

Product is record
Product purpose "One product for sale; its SKU is the catalog's key (the first field)"
Product typeParameter none
Product field sku Int64
Product field unitCents Int64
Product field category String

catalog is table
catalog purpose "Every product for sale and its unit price, looked up by SKU"
catalog rowType Product
catalog row widgetProduct 1
catalog row gadgetProduct 2
catalog row gizmoProduct 3
catalog row sprocketProduct 4
catalog cell widgetProduct sku 101
catalog cell widgetProduct category "hardware"
catalog cell widgetProduct unitCents 250
catalog cell gadgetProduct sku 102
catalog cell gadgetProduct category "electronics"
catalog cell gadgetProduct unitCents 1200
catalog cell gizmoProduct sku 103
catalog cell gizmoProduct category "consumables"
catalog cell gizmoProduct unitCents 35
catalog cell sprocketProduct sku 104
catalog cell sprocketProduct category "hardware"
catalog cell sprocketProduct unitCents 90

Component is record
Component purpose "One part of a bundle: which bundle, which part, and how many of it"
Component typeParameter none
Component field bundleSku Int64
Component field partSku Int64
Component field count Int64

components is table
components purpose "The bill of materials: each bundle's parts; a part may itself be a bundle"
components rowType Component
components row kitWidgets 1
components row kitGadget 2
components row starterKit 3
components row starterGizmos 4
components cell kitWidgets bundleSku 200
components cell kitWidgets partSku 101
components cell kitWidgets count 2
components cell kitGadget bundleSku 200
components cell kitGadget partSku 102
components cell kitGadget count 1
components cell starterKit bundleSku 300
components cell starterKit partSku 200
components cell starterKit count 1
components cell starterGizmos bundleSku 300
components cell starterGizmos partSku 103
components cell starterGizmos count 5

OrderError is enum
OrderError purpose "Why one order line could not be turned into priced parts"
OrderError typeParameter none
OrderError variant unknownProduct Int64
OrderError variant tooDeep Int64

CategoryTotals is typeInstance
CategoryTotals purpose "Cents at list price per category name, in the order categories first appear"
CategoryTotals in none
CategoryTotals instantiates map.Map String Int64

SeenSkus is typeInstance
SeenSkus purpose "The SKUs the order has named so far"
SeenSkus in none
SeenSkus instantiates set.Set Int64

SeenItems is typeInstance
SeenItems purpose "The items markNew has been given"
SeenItems in markNew
SeenItems instantiates set.Set T

markSku is operationInstance
markSku purpose "markNew for SKUs"
markSku in none
markSku instantiates markNew Int64

order is table
order purpose "The order to price, one row per line"
order rowType OrderLine
order row widget 1
order row gadget 2
order row gizmo 3
order row starter 4
order cell widget sku 101
order cell widget quantity 4
order cell gadget sku 102
order cell gadget quantity 2
order cell gizmo sku 103
order cell gizmo quantity 10
order cell starter sku 300
order cell starter quantity 1

